On HP with TCB (trusted computer base) there is a way:
/usr/lbin/modprpw -k <username>
I'm not sure about SCO. You may try this, but I can't guarantee.

Instead of this, use your favourite $EDITOR to edit ONE file (yes, it
WORKS!). TCB of users is stored under /tcb directory... Edit a file with
name: /tcb/files/auth/<first_letter_of_login_name>/<login_name>

You will find (at the end of the file) string, which looks like:
"u_lock@:chkent:".

Unlocked accounts have string ":ulock@:", locked accounts have
":ulock:". Add/delete just "@" to (dis)allow interactive logins.

HTH,

