Hi all;

expanding advfs root by adding another volume is bad for a number of reasons --
/usr is also a bad idea.

The reason it cant be supported for root (besides the mtbf for root decreasing)
is that recovery would be a nightmare -- addvol is not on the CD - it is in
/usr/sbin (which addvol'ing /usr, while doable, is a very bad idea).  The
kicker really is that addvol requires the advfs advanced utils license to be
active -- and this doesnt happen until you hit multiuser mode ! (the license db
is loaded from /var/adm/lmf).

Just a couple of thoughts...

Duane Cady
Compaq Computer Corp.




