One of the "gotchas" I have experienced in Y2K testing is with Database
programs.  They do not like to be running when dates get moved into far
future or backwards.  I would recommend that you make sure to use test
data and not live data and always shutdown the database before changing
the date.


Also, if cron is running when you change the date, all cron processes
will kick off to try and catch up.

