Adrian (adrian@harcourt.ndirect.co.uk) wrote:
: I'm trying to backup the root partition, when booted from a CD. I can
: mount another disk and dump to that, but when I try to dump to tape I
: get the error "Available blocks (74) is less than estimated blocks
: (50635)". The command I'm using is "dump -0f /dev/rmt2h /dev/rz3a". I'm
: using a new tape, and I can run the command OK when booted from disk.
: Any idea what I'm doing wrong?

After booting from CD, but before starting the dump command, look at your
/dev/ directory and see if you have a /dev/rmt2h device special file.  If not,
then what you're doing is attempting to dump to a file named /dev/rmt2h, not
to the device.

You'll probably need to take note of the device name from the hardware
inventory at boot time (something like tz5), then type the command:

        # /dev/MAKEDEV tz5
        
which will then create the needed device special files.

        Stu



