lih-sin the wrote:

> Hi,
>
>   we just install RH 6.0 on an Intel PentiumPro200, however
> when we want to nsf mount the /home partition by DU/OSF
> machine, RH 6.0 gives us an error message:
>
> "NFS3 RFS3_GETATTR failed for server photon: RPC: Program/version mismatch
> photon on /photon/xte: I/O error"
>
> where photon is the name of the RH6.0 Intel machine and
> the mount command was sent from Digital UNIX V4.0A and also tried
> from DEC OSF/1 V3.2A.
>
> Before we upgrade to RH6.0, the intel machine ran with RH 5.2,
> and the nsf command worked.
>
> If we sent the nsf mount command from a DECstation3100 running ULTRIX 4.2
> or from a DECAlpha RH5.2, the command works without a problem.
>
> could you tell me how i fix this problem?

I've found that RH6.0 has problems dealing with clients
that make NFS V3 mount requests. I thought the
version was supposed to be negotiated, but
Linux NFS doesn't seem to be aware of this ;^)

On Solaris, I solved this by explicitly requesting
V2 in the mount command:

# mount -o vers=2 host:/home /home

There's some equivalent for the Digital UNIX mount
command. It's probably the same.

Jeff
