Rob Derstadt wrote:

> Hello,
>
> I'd like to load a library at runtime using dlopen(...) and dlsym(...)
> on an alpha running OSF1. I'm using cc and am not sure what
> compiler/linker flags I need to use, does anyone know? Also, is there a
> way to tell if the library I'd like to open is indeed loadable at
> runtime? It's a 3rd part lib that I don't have source access to. Thanks
> in advance.

From a compilation standpoint, the only requirement that I know
of is that the program that wants to use dlopen() must
be linked shared itself, that is, with -call_shared not -static.
Because shared linking is the default, you don't need to do
anything.

As for the second part of your question, there's no real way
to tell if you can load a library successfully without trying.
Check the return status of your calls and be sure to code
a nice failure path ;^) Seriously, a quick little program will
tell you whether the library you have in mind will cooperate.

