We also found the -check option to be too noisy in V4.0D and
earlier, so we added quite a few new features (see below).

You can use the new features of the latest Compaq C compiler on
your V4.0D-F system by installing the compiler in the Developers'
Toolkit. That is, you can update your compiler and development
tools without upgrading your OS. The Developers' Toolkit is
currently in field test and is expected out in the early fall
of this year.

For more info, see
  http://www.unix.digital.com/developerstoolkit/

In the new compilers for V4.0E and later, there is much better
user control over the messages. You can enable/disable individual
messages or groups of messages via the command line or #pragmas.
These are described in the cc(1) man page (look for the -msg_ flags).

Also, the messages generated in "system header files", which are
generally files that you do not control, will be quieted by default.
This is described in the cc(1) man page (look for the -SD flag)

We've also worked closely with many developers, including our UNIX
development community, to help tailor the diagnostics that come
out by default. New diagnostics have also been added for things
like uninitialized variables and also 64-bit porting issues. So
far, we've received very good feedback.

-Jeff
