My 2nd method is:


1. HP JETDIRECT network adapters use the tcp port 9100.
    Create in yor /etc/services file:

jdp_9100       9100/tcp                # Added for HP-Printer JetDirect cards

2. Edit the /etc/hosts  file:

123.45.67.89 my_printer             # printer on JETDIRECT

3. Edit your /etc/printcap file:

my_printer:\
        :ct=tcp:\
        :if=/usr/lbin/ps_level1of:\
        :lf=/var/spool/lpd/my_printer/log:\
        :lp=@my_printer/jdp_9100:\
        :mx#0:\
        :pl#72:\
        :pw#80:\
        :rw:\
        :of=/usr/lbin/ps_level1of:\
        :sd=/var/spool/lpd/my_printer:\
        :sh:

4. Create the /var/spool/lpd/my_printer

Thats all, and its work fine. All lpr Kommands eg. -#n or -K2 ... are
supported.

Joerg-Uwe


