In article <3753D879.B1062E0E@ulg.ac.be>,
Nguyen-Dai Quy  <Daiquy.Nguyen@ulg.ac.be> wrote:
>I compiled ssh-1.2.27 without error. After run shhd, I try connect from
>RH box or Digital Unix station (both shh-2.x) but it not works.

You cannot connect from a v2 client to a v1 server.

>2) From RH-5.2 (ssh-2.x, client) to HP-UX 10.20 (ssh-1.x)

Same here.

>3) from HP-UX (ssh-1.x client) to RH-5.2 (ssh-2.x) or Digital Unix
>(ssh-2.x) :

This will only work if you configure the ssh v2 server to pass off
the connection to a copy of the ssh v1 server.  You'll need v1.2.26 or
better for this to work.  You need the following lines in your v2
sshd2_config file:

        Ssh1Compatibility               yes
        Sshd1Path                       path-to-sshd-v1-server

>PS: I can not compile SSH-2 on HP-UX 10.20 !!!

Then you need the ssh v1 client on your other systems to connect to
the HP system.


