Dennis Breeden wrote in message <374F012B.4C1741BC@mci.com>...
>I have installed 2 PBXGB-AA video cards in a DEC ALPHAStation 500/333.
>I got the system to final boot up and regen the kernal.  I have been
>unable to export any displays to the second card. i.e. xclock -display
>localhost:1.0 (or 0.1).  I tried putting a second entry in Xservers, but
>this did not help.  I know I am missing something.  Help

Hi
Beware of the jumper settings on the card, the jumper marked VGA should be
'on' on at most one card in the system. The alias jumper should be the same
on on both cards.

At the console prompt type show config, does the card show up there ?
If no then you have a hardware problem (Card not seated? Jumpers not
correct?)

If yes, then boot from the generic kernel (boot -file genvmunix)
Watch the boot process, look out for TGA graphics cards (You should see
two).
When the system comes up you should have graphics on both heads.
Rebuild the kernel using doconfig.
copy this kernel to /
sync the disks and reboot.

When you want to address the second head you address it as localhost:0.1
(You have one X server with two screens)

Hope this helps
Adam
