Dennis Breeden wrote:
> 
> I have installed 2 PBXGB-AA video cards in a DEC ALPHAStation 500/333.
> I got the system to final boot up and regen the kernal.  I have been
> unable to export any displays to the second card. i.e. xclock -display
> localhost:1.0 (or 0.1).

The correct screen will be 0.1 when this works.  1.0 gives you the
second
server, which doesn't exist.

First, do 'sizer -gt' as root.  This is a low-level test to see if the
kernel recognizes both cards.  If you don't have two entries, then you
need to do some kernel configuration work to get the second card
recognized.

If the second card is recognized but you still don't have a second X
screen,
do 'xdpyinfo' on the system and look for information about a second
screen.  If it's missing, server configuration is needed.  Check
/var/dt/Xerrors
(if you're using cde) for hints as to any problems.  Then visit
/var/X11/Xserver.conf.  In particular, look for any '-onlyScreen'
options
that would disable a second screen.

Also recommended is having all graphics cards on PCI bus 0, when
possible
and may be required with some system/card combinations.  This can be 
checked at console or in /var/adm/messages.


