I am not certain what contributes to your speed difference,
but I write all kinds of number crunching float/int operations
under Dec Unix. I ocassionally try to optimize once for gcc and
once for cc. I cannot beat cc for speed. Typically I get
15-20% speed differences. 

However, I also find subtle differences in the parsing of
the compilers, and I am either more used to gcc, or it is
more bug free, because I continue to use it. Things like
typecasting of arguments tend to get me in much more trouble
using cc than gcc.

